  "tips": [
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l15-a5-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l15-a5-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Ćwierć kilo białego sera"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "At the counter the seller says *słucham?* (yes, please?). An adjective after a container is in the genitive too: *słoik dżemu malinowego* (a jar of raspberry jam), *kawałek żółtego sera* (a piece of hard cheese), *ćwierć kilo białego sera* (a quarter of a kilo of curd cheese), *paczka czarnej herbaty*. *Jeszcze poproszę…* asks for one more thing."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l15-a5-t02",
      "before": "kpk1-l15-a5-e08",
      "title": {
        "en": "Gram, gramy, gramów"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "*Ćwierć kilo* is 250 grams. One *gram*; after *dwa*, *trzy* and *cztery*, *gramy*; from *pięć* to *dwadzieścia jeden*, *gramów*: *dwadzieścia gramów*. Part B shows that most words count this way."
      }
    }
  ],
